        ],
        "text": "The statute defines \u201cserious or violent\u201d felonies and makes a third felony trigger the three\u2011strike sentence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, one question before the Court was whether it is unreasonable to impose a life sentence on a defendant with a record of non\u2011violent offenses."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-64b94292e9cd-0002-0000",
              "ev-64b94292e9cd-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, justices also asked whether the statute\u2019s seriousness requirement could be satisfied by a series of thefts or by multiple prior speeding offenses classified as felonies."
      }
    ],
